From 75e91e62d3a2d454709891c55ce0397d2ec72554 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rieki777 <rieki@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 13:59:43 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(quest): path portals + citizenship tier sidebar +
 moss-ruin locked cards (Phase 3)

Phase 3 of QUEST_PAGE_AND_PATH_PROGRESSION_SPEC.md. The /quest page
gains the four-portal selector for path filtering, a horizontal
citizenship tier sidebar above the portals, and the locked-quest card
is redesigned per spec section 9.8 as a moss-overgrown stone ruin
with a bioluminescent elemental glyph instead of a corporate lock
icon.

New components:
  - PathPortalsSelector: four elemental portals (fire/water/earth/air
    mapped to player/investor/land_project/ally). Hollow Knight-style
    fade-in shimmer on first paint. Declared paths render filled with
    aurora glow; undeclared render as outline silhouettes that route
    to /profile?tab=quests when tapped (where the existing Add a Path
    modal lives).
  - CitizenshipTierSidebar: vertical timeline + horizontal pill
    variants. Player's current rung pulses; next rung shows faintly.
    Tap-targets scroll to the matching page section.
  - LockedQuestCard: complete rewrite. SVG silhouette of a ruined
    stone arch with moss creeping up from the base, plus an inline
    bioluminescent glyph centered in the arch. Backward compatible
    prop API so existing call-sites keep working.

Integration:
  - Quest.tsx adds <PathProgressionSection> directly below the hero,
    rendering the tier sidebar in a header row plus the four portals
    below. Reads from the Phase 2 playerPaths.getMyPaths query.

Deferred to Phase 3.1: hero-card treatment for threshold quests, the
canopy-fall unlock animation, and the Open Universe two-at-a-time
reveal logic. Those need quest-pool tagging on existing data and
minor Quest.tsx layout work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
